  "limits": [
    "Short headless FPS samples do not guarantee identical performance on physical hardware.",
    "The stress scene intentionally drives attacks every 130ms and can advance many foes per hit; it was already below 60 FPS before this change. It improved here from 47 to 55 FPS.",
    "The before stress probe used a conditional against encounterHold, which does not exist in the old runtime, so every probe ran. The final probe dispatches every input unconditionally, preserving the same input rate.",
    "The replay comparison suppresses impact-decoration RNG equally in both versions to isolate identical seeded gameplay RNG; it checks the actual loot/currency/progression functions.",
    "No CPU soak claim is made for the new atmosphere. New animations are CSS/WAAPI, finite UI transitions reuse nodes, and long ambient loops do not modify the DOM.",
    "Phone/380px/touch QA remains deferred to round 5. New atmospheric motion is desktop only."
